.\" sysstat.pcpconf.5 - Manual page for the sysstat PCP local metric config file
.TH SYSSTAT.PCPCONF 5 "JUNE 2026" "sysstat-@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "Linux User's Manual" -*- nroff -*-
.SH NAME
sysstat.pcpconf \- sysstat PCP local metric collection configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sysstat.pcpconf
file configures which additional metrics
.BR sadc (8)
records from a local PMDA context when writing PCP archives
(via
.B \-O pcp
or
.BR "\-O sa+pcp" ).
It is read once at
.B sadc
startup; changes take effect on the next restart.
.PP
The default location is
.IR @SYSCONFIG_DIR@/sysstat.pcpconf .
The
.B SYSSTAT_PCPCONF
environment variable overrides this path.
.SH "FILE FORMAT"
The file uses a simple INI-style format.  Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.  Blank lines are ignored.
.SS "Global settings"
Key\-value pairs (separated by
.BR = )
before the first section heading are treated as global settings.
.TP
.BI "volume_size = " size
Maximum PCP data volume size before automatic rotation.
Accepts an optional
.BR k ", " m " or " g
suffix for kibibytes, mebibytes or gibibytes respectively.
Set to 0 to disable in-session rotation.  Default: 0.
.SS "Metric groups"
Each
.BI [ NAME ]
section heading starts a named metric group.  One metric name per line
within the section.  Both leaf metric names
(e.g.\&
.IR proc.psinfo.pid )
and namespace node names
(e.g.\&
.IR proc.psinfo )
are accepted; namespace nodes are expanded to all leaf metrics beneath them.
.PP
Group names are uppercased internally and can be used with
.BR sadc 's
.B \-S
option to selectively enable collection (e.g.\&
.BR "\-S PROC" ).
By default, groups are disabled; they are enabled by
.BR "\-S ALL" " or " "\-S XALL" .
.PP
Metrics whose PMID is already registered by
.BR sadc 's
built-in write path are silently skipped to avoid double-writes.
Unknown metric names are skipped with a warning on stderr.
.PP
To list all metrics available from the local PMDA context, run:
.PP
.RS
.B pminfo \-L
.RE
.PP
To inspect a specific metric or subtree (e.g. for description and units), run:
.PP
.RS
.B pminfo \-L \-\-desc \-\-oneline proc.psinfo
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# Global settings (before any [heading])
volume_size = 100m

[PROC]
proc.nprocs
proc.psinfo.utime
proc.psinfo.stime
proc.psinfo.vsize
proc.psinfo.rss
proc.io.read_bytes
proc.io.write_bytes

[TAPE]
tape.dev.read_cnt
tape.dev.write_cnt

[IOSTAT]
disk.dev.read
disk.dev.write
disk.dev.total_bytes

[CIFS]
cifs.fs.read
cifs.fs.write
.fi
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
.TP
.B SYSSTAT_PCPCONF
Overrides the configuration file path.  Useful for testing or
site-specific deployments.
.SH FILES
.I @SYSCONFIG_DIR@/sysstat.pcpconf
.RS
Default configuration file location.
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sadc (8),
.BR sa1 (8),
.BR sa2 (8),
.BR sysstat (5),
.BR pminfo (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sebastien Godard (sysstat <at> orange.fr)
